Usage: touch [OPTION]... FILE...

Update the access and modification times of each FILE to the current time.
A FILE argument that does not exist is created empty, unless -c or -h is supplied.

OPTIONS:
  -a                    change only the access time
  -c, --no-create       do not create any files
  -d, --date ARG        parse STRING and use it instead of current time
  -f                    (ignored)
  -h, --no-dereference  affect symbolic link instead of referenced file
  -m                    change only the modification time
  -r, --reference ARG   use this file's times instead of current time
  -t ARG                use [[CC]YY]MMDDhhmm[.ss] instead of current time
      --time ARG        change the specified time
                        (access/atime/use/modify/mtime)
      --help            display this help and exit
  -V, --version         output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
